  "term": "tunnel vision",
  "definition": "Tunnel vision is severe loss of the peripheral visual field, so vision is largely limited to a narrower central area. In the supplied source, it is described as occurring in degenerative retinal disease and as reducing peripheral information needed for scanning and mobility.",
